title: 'False positive: array parameters rejected for &inout (Only object types that support object handles can use &inout)'
updated_at: "2026-09-09T03:09:14Z"
---
False positive: the game compiler accepts `&inout` on script array parameters; openplanet-lsp rejects them.

## Repro (minimal, standalone plugin)

`Main.as`:

    void ApplyClassToEntries(int[] &inout classes, const int[] &in entryIxs, int cls) {
        for (uint i = 0; i < entryIxs.Length; i++) classes[uint(entryIxs[i])] = cls;
    }

    void CoalesceStrings(string[] &inout messages, const string &in m) {
        messages.InsertLast(m);
    }

    void UseThem() {
        int[] a = {1,2,3};
        int[] ix = {0};
        ApplyClassToEntries(a, ix, 7);
        string[] s;
        CoalesceStrings(s, "x");
    }

Command:

    openplanet-lsp check --plugins-dir ~/OpenplanetNext/Plugins <dir>

## LSP reports

    Main.as:1:26: error: Only object types that support object handles can use &inout. Use &in or &out instead.
    Main.as:5:22: error: Only object types that support object handles can use &inout. Use &in or &out instead.

## Reality

`array<T>` is a reference type that supports handles (`array<int>@`), so `&inout` is legal.
Verified game-side on Openplanet 1.29.14: tm-editor-plus-plus contains both shapes
(`src/Components/Map/LmQualityTuner.as:1285` `int[] &inout classes`,
`src/FromML.as:137` `ML_Event@[] &inout messages`) and compiles + loads cleanly
(remote build 2026-09-09 09:24, "Build: 1059.67 ms", plugin loaded).

## Expected

No diagnostic for `&inout` on script array types (`T[]` / `array<T>`), including
arrays of handles (`ML_Event@[] &inout`). The rule should only fire for value types
that genuinely do not support handles (primitives, `vec3`, etc).

Found while checking tm-editor-plus-plus; blocks its `build.sh` (which gates on
`openplanet-lsp check`) and forced an `EPP_SKIP_LSP=1` bypass.